High-end integrated circuit (IC) substrates are critical interconnect structures that connect semiconductor dies to package-level circuitry and external systems. As processors and other advanced chips integrate more functions, substrate design becomes increasingly important for signal integrity, power delivery, thermal management, and the physical integration of high-performance semiconductor packages.

